---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import Stitch from "../components/Stitch.astro";
import PillarCard from "../components/PillarCard.astro";
---

<Page
	title="Automate Ethically"
	description="A movement for automation with a human in the loop: laws that keep a person accountable for every automated decision, software built on that principle, and help retraining for durable work."
>
		<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 1: hero headline + subhead -->
		<section class="ae-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
			<p class="ae-eyebrow">A movement for ethical automation</p>
			<h1 id="hero-title">A human makes the decision.</h1>
			<p class="ae-hero-sub">
				Cameras watch your street. Machines answer your insurance claim. Data
				centers rise at the edge of town. None of them can be held accountable
				— only a person can. We want one rule, everywhere it matters:
				<strong>a human makes the decision, and answers for it.</strong>
			</p>
			<p class="ae-hero-urgent">
				The laws are being written right now — 45 states are debating them
				this session. The rulebook gets set with you, or without you.
			</p>
			<figure class="ae-epigraph">
				<blockquote>
					The loom did not remove the weaver. A person still chose the pattern,
					punched the cards, examined the cloth, and signed the bolt.
				</blockquote>
				<figcaption>jacquard, 1804 — and the rule we intend to keep</figcaption>
			</figure>
			<div class="ae-cta-row">
				<a class="ae-btn ae-btn--primary" href="/act">Take action</a>
				<a class="ae-btn ae-btn--ghost" href="#manifesto">Read the manifesto</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<Stitch />

		<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 2: manifesto -->
		<section class="ae-section" id="manifesto" aria-labelledby="manifesto-title">
			<div class="ae-container">
				<p class="ae-eyebrow">Why now</p>
				<h2 class="ae-h2" id="manifesto-title">
					The anger is real. Aim it at the rulebook.
				</h2>
				<div class="ae-prose">
					<p>
						You are right to be angry. The cameras went up without asking you.
						The data center got its permits before you heard about it. The
						machine denied the claim, and no one's name was on the denial.
					</p>
					<p>
						But a data center is a totem. Block one, and the machines it
						served move one county over. The win that lasts is a law: wherever
						an automated system touches your life, a person decides — and that
						person answers for it.
					</p>
					<p>
						Machines cannot take responsibility. Companies will not volunteer
						it. Rules change when neighbors organize — city by city, then
						state by state. That is how it has always worked.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<Stitch />

		<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 11: urgency stats framing (numbers + citations stay; see FACTS.md) -->
		<section class="ae-section" id="clock" aria-labelledby="clock-title">
			<div class="ae-container">
				<p class="ae-eyebrow">Right now</p>
				<h2 class="ae-h2" id="clock-title">The clock is the rulebook</h2>
				<p class="ae-hero-sub">
					None of this is hypothetical. It is already on your street, your
					power bill, and your legislature's calendar.
				</p>
				<div class="ae-stats">
					<div class="ae-stat">
						<span class="ae-stat-num">6,000</span>
						<span class="ae-stat-label">
							communities watched by one company's license-plate cameras,
							across 49 states
						</span>
						<span class="ae-stat-src">
							<a href="https://www.ipm.org/news/2026-08-17/flock-safety-tightens-safeguards-as-states-cities-question-surveillance-network">Stateline</a>, Aug 2026
						</span>
					</div>
					<div class="ae-stat">
						<span class="ae-stat-num">426&thinsp;TWh</span>
						<span class="ae-stat-label">
							projected US data-center electricity by 2030 — more than double
							2024, and nearly half of all US demand growth
						</span>
						<span class="ae-stat-src">
							<a href="https://www.iea.org/reports/energy-and-ai/energy-demand-from-ai">IEA, Energy and AI</a>
						</span>
					</div>
					<div class="ae-stat">
						<span class="ae-stat-num">1,561</span>
						<span class="ae-stat-label">
							AI bills introduced in 45 states this session — the rules are
							being written with you or without you
						</span>
						<span class="ae-stat-src">
							<a href="https://www.multistate.ai/artificial-intelligence-ai-legislation">multistate.ai</a>, Mar 2026
						</span>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="ae-aside">
					It can go the right way: more than 50 communities have already
					paused or canceled camera contracts since January
					(<a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/02/17/nx-s1-5612825/flock-contracts-canceled-immigration-survillance-concerns">NPR</a>),
					and Montana already requires a human to review AI-driven agency
					decisions. Facts checked Aug 2026 — sources and our correction
					policy live in the open at
					<a href="/facts">FACTS.md</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<Stitch />

		<section class="ae-section ae-section--tint" id="pillars" aria-labelledby="pillars-title">
			<div class="ae-container">
				<p class="ae-eyebrow">The work</p>
				<h2 class="ae-h2" id="pillars-title">Three pillars, one principle</h2>
				<div class="ae-pillars">
					<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 3: pillar Organize -->
					<PillarCard title="Organize" chip="organizing now" id="organize">
						<p>
							Start where the decisions are made: city councils, county boards,
							school boards. Ask for one ordinance:
							<strong>an automation may act, but a person decides — and that
							person is accountable.</strong> Then carry it to the state house.
						</p>
						<p><a href="/act">See how to get started &rarr;</a></p>
					</PillarCard>
					<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 4: pillar Build ethically -->
					<PillarCard title="Build ethically" chip="software below" id="build">
						<p>
							Policy asks people to behave. Software can make the rule
							physical. We build tools where
							<strong>accountability is enforced by the build itself</strong> —
							a machine can propose, but it cannot sign.
						</p>
						<p><a href="/about#projects">See what we're building &rarr;</a></p>
					</PillarCard>
					<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 5: pillar Retrain -->
					<PillarCard title="Retrain" chip="coming" chipQuiet id="retrain">
						<p>
							The honest answer to "there will always be more work" is a
							coordination layer that helps people
							<strong>learn the next field while they still have this
							job</strong> — from the office, from home, before the pink slip.
							Without that layer, optimism becomes cruelty.
						</p>
					</PillarCard>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<Stitch />

		<section class="ae-section ae-section--tint" aria-labelledby="about-pointer-title">
			<div class="ae-container">
				<p class="ae-eyebrow">The movement</p>
				<h2 class="ae-h2" id="about-pointer-title">Neighbors, builders, and organizers.</h2>
				<p class="ae-plain">
					We intend to form a registered political committee. Until that
					exists, we are not asking for money.
				</p>
				<p class="ae-aside">
					<a href="/about">Who's behind this, and the software we're
					building alongside it &rarr;</a>
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 23: index action band replacing get-involved -->
		<section class="ae-section" id="get-involved" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
			<div class="ae-container">
				<p class="ae-eyebrow">Get involved</p>
				<h2 class="ae-h2" id="cta-title">Your town writes rules this year. Be in the room.</h2>
				<p class="ae-plain">
					Pick the rung you can reach today — thirty seconds or an hour, every
					bit of it counts. Most ordinances pass in rooms with ten people in
					them.
				</p>
				<div class="ae-cta-row">
					<a class="ae-btn ae-btn--primary" href="/act#join">Join the list</a>
					<a class="ae-btn ae-btn--ghost" href="/act#petition">Sign the petition</a>
				</div>
				<p class="ae-aside">
					<a href="/act">See every way to help &rarr;</a>
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<div class="ae-coda">
			<p>
				&ldquo;Physics was the easy part. Everyone still has to become
				different at the same time, and everyone has a reason to go
				last.&rdquo;
			</p>
		</div>
</Page>
